# Storm Architecture Rules

## Shell Routing (page.tsx)

`page.tsx` is routing only — no business logic, no inline UI. It maps `userRole` to a shell component:

| Role | Shell | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `candidate` | `CandidateShell` | **Primary.** All new features go here. Uses composable blocks. |
| `employer` | `EmployerShell` | Employer-specific features (job posting, talent search, etc.) |
| `driver` | `DriverShell` | **Legacy only.** Existing users who haven't migrated. Do NOT add new features here. |
| `developer` | `DeveloperShell` | **Legacy only.** Same as above. |

### Rules

- **All new candidate features go in `CandidateShell` via blocks.** Never add features to `DriverShell` or `DeveloperShell`.
- **`DriverShell` and `DeveloperShell` are frozen.** They exist for backward compatibility. Do not extend them.
- **Shells route; they don't build UI.** A shell switches on `currentPage` and returns the right component. It does not contain JSX for those features.
- **When `CandidateShell` exceeds ~200 lines (~14 routes):** Refactor the `if/if/if` chain into a route map object (`Record<PageType, ComponentType>`). Standardize block page components to accept a common `{ onBack }` prop so they can be rendered from the map without per-route wrappers.

## Component Structure

Every feature must live in its own component.

```
src/
  app/page.tsx              ← routing + auth + global layout ONLY (~300 lines max)
  components/
    app/                    ← shells and feature flows
      CandidateShell.tsx    ← primary candidate routing (composable blocks)
      EmployerShell.tsx     ← employer routing
      DriverShell.tsx       ← LEGACY — do not extend
      DeveloperShell.tsx    ← LEGACY — do not extend
      ErrorBoundary.tsx
    blocks/                 ← block components for the composable hub
    ui/                     ← reusable primitives (Button, Card, BlockCard, etc.)
    [Feature].tsx           ← standalone feature components
```

### Rules

- **No inline feature rendering in shells.** If a page block exceeds ~30 lines, extract it to a component.
- **One concern per file.** A component renders one feature — not multiple unrelated sections.

```tsx
// BAD — feature logic inline in shell
if (currentPage === 'resume') {
  return (
    <div>
      <ResumeTabSelector ... />
      {resumeTab === 'upload' && <ResumeUploadWithVerification ... />}
      {resumeTab === 'create' && <ResumeBuilder ... />}
    </div>
  )
}

// GOOD — delegate to a dedicated component
if (currentPage === 'resume') {
  return <DriverResumeSection onBack={handleNavigateToHub} />
}
```

