## Notification & Email Patterns

### In-app notifications

Use `createNotification()` from `src/lib/create-notification.ts`. Every notification should have:

- `type` — one of the `NotificationType` values
- `title` + `body` — human-readable
- `actionUrl` — where bell-click navigates (use `/?onboard={pageRoute}` for block deep-links)
- `data` — structured metadata for programmatic use

When adding a new notification type, add it to the `NotificationType` union in `create-notification.ts` and handle it in `NotificationBell.tsx` (icon + color).

### Emails

| Path | Template | How it works |
|---|---|---|
| Invite outreach | `src/lib/send-invite-email.ts` | Auto-reads `label` + `description` from block registry. No per-block template needed. |
| Request/recruit | `src/lib/send-admin-notification.ts` | Uses `requestType` + `blockLabel` for copy. Add new `requestType` entries to `REQUEST_TYPE_LABELS` and `REQUEST_ACTION_TEXT`. |
| Admin alerts | `src/lib/send-admin-notification.ts` | For admin-facing notifications (new company, etc.) |

When adding a new email type, add it to the appropriate file above. Never create a one-off email sender — reuse the shared HTML wrapper functions (`detailsBox`, `infoBox`, `ctaButton`).

